  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f_k(n)$ be minimal such that if $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ have no $k+1$ points on a line then there must be at most $f_k(n)$ many lines containing at least $k$ points. Is it true that $ f_k(n)=o(n^2) $ for $k\\geq 4$?",
